{"timestamp":"2026-05-19T17:57:17.841Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"{\"findings\":[{\"title\":\"JSON-escaped secrets can survive JSONL redaction\",\"category\":\"security\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"redact/redact.go\",\"startLine\":562,\"endLine\":579,\"symbol\":\"applyJSONReplacements\",\"quote\":\"origJSON, err := jsonEncodeString(r.original)\"},{\"path\":\"redact/redact.go\",\"startLine\":616,\"endLine\":619,\"symbol\":\"replaceKeyedJSONValue\",\"quote\":\"if p+len(origJSON) <= len(s) && s[p:p+len(origJSON)] == origJSON {\"},{\"path\":\"redact/redact.go\",\"startLine\":728,\"endLine\":736,\"symbol\":\"jsonEncodeString\",\"quote\":\"enc.SetEscapeHTML(false)\"}],\"reasoning\":\"JSONLContent decodes JSON values, decides a decoded string needs redaction, then tries to replace one canonical JSON spelling of that decoded string in the original bytes. Valid JSON can spell the same secret with escapes, for example an AWS key containing `\\\\u0059` for `Y`. The decoded value is detected, but the raw value does not equal the canonical string produced by jsonEncodeString, so replaceKeyedJSONValue leaves the original escaped secret in place.\",\"reproduction\":\"JSONLContent(`{\\\"content\\\":\\\"AKIA\\\\u0059RWQG5EJLPZLBYNP\\\"}`) decodes the value to `AKIAYRWQG5EJLPZLBYNP`, but searches for the unescaped JSON literal, so the escaped AWS key remains in output.\",\"recommendation\":\"Replace JSON string values by raw byte span rather than by canonical string search. A minimal fix is to have the keyed replacement parse the string literal after the key, decode it for comparison, and replace the exact raw literal span with replJSON. A more robust fix is to collect value spans while tokenizing JSON.\",\"whyTestsDoNotAlreadyCoverThis\":\"Existing JSONL tests use literals produced in the same canonical form that jsonEncodeString emits; they do not cover semantically equivalent JSON strings with unicode, slash, or HTML-style escapes.\",\"suggestedRegressionTest\":\"Add a JSONLContent test with an escaped secret such as `{\\\"content\\\":\\\"AKIA\\\\u0059RWQG5EJLPZLBYNP\\\"}` and assert neither the raw escape sequence nor the decoded key remains.\",\"minimumFixScope\":\"redact/redact.go JSON replacement path plus JSONLContent regression coverage.\"},{\"title\":\"Generic JSON password fields with low-entropy values are not redacted outside DB-shaped objects\",\"category\":\"security\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"redact/redact.go\",\"startLine\":443,\"endLine\":448,\"symbol\":\"isCredentialJSONSecretKey\",\"quote\":\"return credentialContext && genericPasswordKeyRegex.MatchString(normalized)\"},{\"path\":\"redact/redact.go\",\"startLine\":664,\"endLine\":668,\"symbol\":\"collectJSONLReplacements\",\"quote\":\"if redacted == val && isCredentialJSONSecretKey(key, credentialContext) && hasNonPlaceholderPasswordValue(val) {\"},{\"path\":\"redact/redact_test.go\",\"startLine\":768,\"endLine\":794,\"symbol\":\"TestJSONLContent_StructuredCredentialFieldsRedacted\",\"quote\":\"`\\\"password\\\":\\\"REDACTED\\\"`\"}],\"reasoning\":\"For JSON string values, low-entropy secrets are only redacted by key when isCredentialJSONSecretKey returns true. DB-prefixed keys are always covered, but exact `password`, `passwd`, or `pwd` keys are only covered when the containing object also looks like a DB credential object with host and user fields. A common payload like `{\\\"password\\\":\\\"correct-horse\\\"}` has no host/user context, the value is too low-entropy for String(val), and the key check returns false, so the password remains in the redacted transcript.\",\"reproduction\":\"JSONLContent(`{\\\"password\\\":\\\"correct-horse\\\"}`) returns the password unchanged because `credentialContext` is false and `correct-horse` is not detected by entropy or vendor patterns.\",\"recommendation\":\"Treat exact JSON keys `password`, `passwd`, and `pwd` as credential secret keys regardless of DB object context, while still applying hasNonPlaceholderPasswordValue to avoid redacting placeholders.\",\"whyTestsDoNotAlreadyCoverThis\":\"The tests cover generic `password` only inside a DB-shaped object with host and user fields, and raw-text `password=...` preservation does not exercise structured JSON key handling.\",\"suggestedRegressionTest\":\"Add JSONLContent cases for `{\\\"password\\\":\\\"correct-horse\\\"}`, `{\\\"pwd\\\":\\\"correct-horse\\\"}`, and placeholder values such as `{\\\"password\\\":\\\"${PASSWORD}\\\"}`.\",\"minimumFixScope\":\"redact/redact.go key classification logic and JSONL credential-field tests.\"}],\"inspected\":{\"files\":[\"redact/custom.go\",\"redact/packs.go\",\"redact/pii.go\",\"redact/redact.go\",\"redact/betterleaks_env_test.go\",\"redact/custom_test.go\",\"redact/packs_test.go\",\"redact/pii_test.go\",\"redact/redact_bench_test.go\",\"redact/redact_test.go\"],\"symbols\":[\"ConfigureCustomRules\",\"detectCustomRules\",\"ParsePack\",\"LoadPacks\",\"ConfigurePII\",\"detectPII\",\"String\",\"JSONLContent\",\"applyJSONReplacements\",\"replaceKeyedJSONValue\",\"collectJSONLReplacements\",\"isCredentialJSONSecretKey\"],\"notes\":[\"Reviewed owned files and linked tests using the code-reviewer workflow.\",\"Did not execute go test: the read-only sandbox prevented Go from creating its temporary build work directory.\"]}}","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
